{"file":"privacy-policy-Bu-PXzVj.js","mappings":";;;;;AACa,QAAA,WAAAA,eAAAC,WAAA,EAAA,OAAM,6BAAyB,MAAA,CAAA,CAAA,u0JAAA;;;;;;;;;","names":["_ssrRenderAttrs","_mergeProps"],"sources":["../../../../app/pages/privacy-policy.vue"],"sourcesContent":["<template>\n    <article class=\"p-5 flex flex-col gap-5\">\n        GHOSTFORM PRIVACY POLICY<br>\nEffective Date: May 15, 2026<br>\nLast Updated: May 15, 2026\n<div>\n1. Introduction & Scope\nWelcome to GhostForm (\"we,\" \"our,\" or \"us\"). GhostForm operates a specialized lead-capture, AI-driven evaluation, and automated notification pipeline (the \"Service\"). This Privacy Policy describes how we collect, secure, process, and share personal information when you use our platform, visit our website, or interact with our automated lead-capture forms (each, a \"GhostForm\").\n\nBy accessing or using the Service, you acknowledge that you have read, understood, and agreed to the practices described in this document.\n</div>\n<div>\n2. Data We Collect and Process\nWe split data collection into two categories: Account Information (data provided by our customers/subscribers) and Lead-Capture Information (data submitted by end-users into a GhostForm).\n\nA. Account Information (Subscribers & Agents)\nIdentity Data: Full name, business name, professional licenses, and email addresses.\n\nBilling & Transactional Data: Payment processing metrics handled securely via our third-party merchant gateway (Stripe). We do not store raw credit card numbers on our local servers.\n\nOperational Data: Custom QR code configurations, unique Node IDs, and deployment metadata.\n\nB. Lead-Capture Information (End Users & Consumers)\nWhen a consumer interacts with a physical or digital GhostForm QR node, we may process:\n\nContact Information: Name, email address, phone number, and physical mailing addresses.\n\nProperty & Financial Metrics: Estimated property value, target acquisition budgets, spatial specifications (square footage), and localized relocation timelines.\n\nVoluntary Input: Any structural parameters, text notes, or descriptions provided directly within form fields.\n</div>\n<div>\n3. Artificial Intelligence (AI) Processing and Analysis\nGhostForm utilizes machine learning and large language models (LLMs) to perform automated qualification profiling (\"Spectral Analysis\").\n\nThe Logic: Input values (e.g., budget-to-value metrics and urgency thresholds) are compiled to calculate an automated Quality Score and Tier assignment.\n\nAnonymization Framework: Before submitting lead payload data to cloud AI evaluation engines, all highly sensitive fields are stripped or tokenized.\n\nNo Selling of Model Data: GhostForm explicitly guarantees that no personal data collected through consumer forms is ever sold or utilized to train external public machine learning models.\n</div>\n<div>\n4. SMS and Automated Dispatch Compliance (A2P 10DLC)\nTo maintain structural compliance with telecommunication provider frameworks, GhostForm strictly regulates automated mobile notifications:\n\nExplicit Consent: Phone numbers collected on behalf of subscribers are exclusively utilized to transmit immediate dispatch alerts if the end-user has explicitly opted into communication.\n\nNo Third-Party Sharing for Marketing: Mobile phone numbers, opt-in consent records, and personal data collected for SMS delivery will never be shared, rented, or sold to third-party affiliates for independent marketing or promotional purposes.\n\nOpt-Out Control: End-users can opt out of automated SMS tracking alerts at any time by replying STOP to any received transmission.\n</div>\n<div>\n5. Data Retention & Archival\nWe preserve personal data only as long as necessary to fulfill operational business requirements or comply with legislative legal frameworks.\n\nAccount Data: Maintained for the entire duration of active platform subscription.\n\nLead Archive Logs: Retained securely inside our encrypted database clusters (MongoDB Atlas) until explicitly deleted, archived, or purged by the account administrator.\n</div>\n<div>\n6. Security Framework\nGhostForm employs industry-standard administrative, physical, and technical safeguards to preserve the confidentiality and structural integrity of incoming data streams:\n\nEncryption at Rest: All data stores utilize AES-256 bit encryption protocols.\n\nEncryption in Transit: All connections force Secure Socket Layers (HTTPS) utilizing TLS 1.3 encryption.\n\nVulnerability Mitigations: Continuous monitoring, active rate-limiting against automated injection attempts, and invisible cloud bot-mitigation engines (Cloudflare Turnstile).\n</div>\n<div>\n7. Global Privacy Rights (GDPR & CCPA/CPRA)\nDepending on your geographical jurisdiction, consumers and business entities retain specific data rights:\n\nThe Right to Access: Request a complete structural export of the personal records we maintain.\n\nThe Right to Erasure (\"Right to be Forgotten\"): Request that we permanently purge personal identifiers from our production systems.\n\nThe Right to Restrict Processing: Object to automated AI-driven tiering evaluation.\n\nTo exercise any of these structural rights, contact our privacy compliance dispatch desk at: privacy@ghostform.com.\n</div>\n    </article>\n</template>"],"version":3}